From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:10:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 102/110] Shift+click into a later block keeps the selection's
 start

The text run where the selection ended took the Shift+click elsewhere
for a click away from the text and cleared the selection, so the
Shift+click started a new one and the start was lost.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/selectable_rich.rs b/src/selectable_rich.rs
index b116b9b..161d076 100644
--- a/src/selectable_rich.rs
+++ b/src/selectable_rich.rs
@@ -761,8 +761,9 @@ where
                     if state.span_pressed.is_some() {
                         shell.capture_event();
                     }
-                } else if is_focus {
-                    // Pressed elsewhere: beside the text, or in the editor of the Split view
+                } else if is_focus && !state.modifiers.shift() {
+                    // Pressed elsewhere: beside the text, or in the editor of the Split view;
+                    // not Shift+click, which extends the selection from its anchor
                     if let Some(message) = select(Action::Clear) {
                         shell.publish(message);
                     }
